%% FIG-M22-05 — The 9-Layer Software Supply Chain Integrity Model
%% Original, course-owned, editable Mermaid source for Essential CS.
flowchart TB
    L1["Layer 1: Resolution Pinning<br/>Exact semantic versions frozen in lockfile<br/><i>Non-guarantee: does not prevent upstream package substitution/deletion</i>"]
    L2["Layer 2: Expected Digest Ownership<br/>Lockfile records expected cryptographic digests governed by trusted repo<br/><i>Non-guarantee: does not verify whether source code is non-malicious</i>"]
    L3["Layer 3: Fetched-Byte Integrity<br/>SHA-256 hash of downloaded artifact matches recorded expected digest<br/><i>Non-guarantee: digest proves byte immutability, NOT publisher identity</i>"]
    L4["Layer 4: Build Reproducibility<br/>Independent rebuild from source produces bit-for-bit identical binary artifact<br/><i>Non-guarantee: reproducibility does not prove source code is safe or bug-free</i>"]
    L5["Layer 5: Signature Verification<br/>Cryptographic signature over package archive verified via public key<br/><i>Non-guarantee: valid signature proves key possession, NOT trustworthiness</i>"]
    L6["Layer 6: Signer Identity Binding<br/>Public key linked to authenticated maintainer identity (X.509 / Sigstore)<br/><i>Non-guarantee: identity proves who signed, NOT that build was untampered</i>"]
    L7["Layer 7: Build/Source Provenance<br/>Verifiable attestation binding artifact SHA-256, source git commit, and builder (SLSA v1.2)<br/><i>Non-guarantee: provenance is merely metadata without a trusted builder</i>"]
    L8["Layer 8: Trusted Builder Assumptions<br/>Build executes on an isolated, hardened, authenticated build infrastructure<br/><i>Non-guarantee: builder cannot protect against compromised upstream source commits</i>"]
    L9["Layer 9: Verifier Policy Enforcement<br/>Local deployment gate rejects any dependency failing provenance, builder, or integrity criteria<br/><i>Non-guarantee: verifier policy requires human judgment on acceptable risk thresholds</i>"]

    L1 --> L2 --> L3 --> L4 --> L5 --> L6 --> L7 --> L8 --> L9

    WARN["Core Supply Chain Axioms:<br/>1. Pinned Version != Pinned Digest (upstream can replace unpinned bytes).<br/>2. Digest != Publisher Identity (hashes verify bytes, not authors).<br/>3. Signature != Trustworthiness (malware can be signed).<br/>4. Provenance is useless without strict Verifier Adoption Policy."]
